WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
Twenty three people in a room.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.310
Bet me two of them share a birthday.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.490
I'm Tanmay Kulkarni,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.450
for Humanitarians AI,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.270
and you'd lose that bet about half the time.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.650
Now keep the group at twenty three,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.430
and take away days.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.070
Squeeze the calendar to ninety days,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.350
and it's ninety five percent.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.730
Squeeze it to one month,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.630
and it's almost certain.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.890
So what decides it?

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:21.540
Not the people,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.510
we kept them.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.810
Not uneven birthdays,

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.270
they move it a tenth of a point.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.270
It's how many days there are.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.310
Here's the rule.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.970
Take the square root of the days.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.520
Multiply by one point two.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.330
Add a half.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.210
For even odds,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.070
a year needs twenty three people.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.170
One month needs seven.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.770
That's why it's twenty three.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.290
The full video shows three things you could change,

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.790
and the one that decides it.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.154
It's on Humanitarians AI.

